From 89ddcfde358a9783ba098a575ce24141df41edb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Casey <4348807+justincasey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:59:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Native fat GEMM for any trellis width; route mixed-K fat
 experts through it

The fused fat-expert kernel (dequant + MMA + output Hadamard, optional token
scatter; from Mia's AI Lab, MIT) only accepted K4 MCG trellises, so on a
tensor-mixed-K pack (K2/K3 experts, per-projection widths) every fat expert
fell back to reconstruct + cuBLAS + a separate Hadamard + index_add, launched
per expert. Template the kernel on K (1..8) and the codebook (3INST/MCG/MUL1),
export EXL3_FAT_GEMM_MAX_K, and run gate, up (fp32, output Hadamard fused) and
down (scatter into the MoE output) through it whenever it covers the expert.
Equivalence vs the fallback on random trellises: 2e-4 relative error for
K2-5 x 3 codebooks, GEMM and scatter. MiniMax-M3.1 2.15bpw TP=2: prefill
884 -> 921 tok/s at 16K-token chunks; 16K needles 3/3; a 12K-token
teacher-forced NLL is now deterministic (6.9241 in three runs) where the
trellis kernel alone varies 7.85-8.25.
